  "description": "Repairs r-def-cursor-dao/err-multi-violation-sql: the INSERT ran without dbFailOnError and R was never read back: success, Errors 0, and so it answered nothing. Errors read; every row of R read through a snapshot (the baseline); Database.Execute of \"INSERT INTO R (ID, Cd, Rq, Vv) VALUES (1, 'r1', Null, -5)\" with dbFailOnError (128) (one row that duplicates the primary key and the unique Cd, omits the required Rq and breaks the validation rule of Vv); Errors read (Count, then Number, Description and Source of each entry); RecordsAffected read; R read through a new snapshot; a snapshot of T opened and closed; Errors read; the same Execute again; Errors read; R read. Asks how many Errors entries and which Number, Description and Source the one failing call leaves, and whether the row was stored. The fixture copy is opened read-write.",
  "callerSurface": "native-idispatch/x64",
  "invokeLcid": 1033,
  "observationRecipe": [
    "clearErrorInfoBefore",
    "excepinfo",
    "deferredFill",
    "errorInfo"
  ],
